  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Odissi: safe water kiosks for corner stores in Senegal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovate - Drinking Water</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Odissi is a decentralised, IoT powered water purification ATM which is designed to be installed in corner stores, allowing clients to fill up containers with clean water at the push of a button, just a stone&#x2019;s throw from their home. With this pilot project, MIYA, an established drinking water enterprise in Senegal and the mother company of this innovation, aims to validate the Senegalese market, test different marketing strategies and determine financial feasibility to define the sustainability of this new business line. Their ultimate goal is thousands of units allowing millions to access affordable quality water.</narrative>
  </description>
